  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The number of alkali metal(s), from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Li</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Cs</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Rb</mi></math> having ionization enthalpy greater than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and forming stable super oxide is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The super oxide <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math> ion is stable only in the presence of large cations <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Rb</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Cs</mi></math>. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Rb</mi></math> have <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>IE</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math>&nbsp;from the table below. Ionisation enthalpy decreases down the group as metallic character increases.<br />&nbsp;</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Metal</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Li</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Na</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Rb</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cs</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>IE</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>KJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>)</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>520</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>496</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>419</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>403</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>376</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>",
